      "text": "Fighter’s Paradise: 2025 Panini Combat Anthology Cards\nNovember 06, 2025\n\nWritten by: Connor Zimmerlee\n\nFighting fans who double as sports card collectors are in luck, as the debut of 2025 Panini Combat Anthology is here. This release features a plethora of thrilling stars ranging across a variety of different disciplines. Each hobby box comes with four packs of 10 cards, and you can look for 20 inserts or parallels plus two autographs per box, on average.\n\nStarting in the squared circle, you can hunt for an assortment of different wrestlers. With a talented crop of current stars headlining the Major League Wrestling portion of the checklist, such as Matt Riddle, Alex Hammerstone, Satoshi Kojima and Mads Krule Krugger, you will find no shortage of must-have talents.\n\nThey aren’t the only superstars to keep an eye out for. Perhaps you prefer to reminisce about some of the all-time greats, including Hulk Hogan and Kurt Angle. Well, this release is also for you, as these stars and other legends of the ring can be yours.\n\nShifting to the octagon, you can look for several notable MMA icons. Each card pulled packs a wallop of a punch, bringing you the same level of excitement you’d get while watching legends like Jon Jones, Chuck Liddell and many others go to work.\n\nJoining their MMA peers in this collection is an outstanding group of PFL talents. While they’re trading blows in the SmartCage, you can add studs such as Francis Ngannou and Usman Nurmagomedov to your growing collection.\n\nRounding out your glimpse into Panini Combat Anthology is a group of phenoms that call the boxing ring home. From legends of the 20th century like Mike Tyson to recent all-time greats in Floyd Mayweather Jr., this release offers a wide range of exciting, hard-hitting names for fans to hunt for.\n\nFrom wrestling and MMA to PFL and boxing, there is something for everyone to anticipate in this release. So be sure to add Panini Combat Anthology cards to your collection and flex some of the sports’ best in collectible form.\n\nAutographs\n,\nMemorabilia\n,\nMixed Martial Arts\n,\nMMA trading cards\n,\nPFL\n,\nProfessional Fighters League\n,\nProfessional Wrestling\nPost navigation\nPrevious Post\nPrevious\nPanini NIL Spotlight: Hometown Hero Ian Jackson Storms to St. John’s\nNext Post\nNext\nEuroLeague Spotlight: Early-Season Stories, Panini Instant Cards",
      "url": "https://blog.paniniamerica.net/fighters-paradise-2025-panini-combat-anthology-cards/"
